  "learningOutcomes": [
    "Use consistent SI units for pump-system measurements.",
    "Interpret pressure, flow, and fluid-property measurements within stated assumptions.",
    "Explain continuity, Bernoulli, and pipe-loss assumptions before applying results.",
    "Interpret pump curves and system curves without inventing manufacturer data.",
    "Identify cavitation and basic pump fault symptoms within safe training boundaries.",
    "Select instrumentation for pressure, flow, temperature, vibration, and status signals using approved source evidence.",
    "Read time-series pump data for trends, alarms, and missing-data limitations.",
    "Distinguish condition monitoring evidence from predictive-maintenance claims.",
    "Explain the purpose and limits of a pump-system digital twin.",
    "Use AI-assisted diagnosis only as reviewed decision support."
  ],
